**Key idea:** every bit-field operation is **shift + mask**. Build a mask of `w = hi - lo + 1` ones; extraction shifts the field down and masks it, insertion clears the field in place and ORs in the shifted, masked value.

Extract `[5:3]` of `0b1101_0110`:

| step | value |
| --- | --- |
| x | 1101 0110 |
| x >> 3 | 0001 1010 |
| mask (w = 3) | 0000 0111 |
| result | 0000 0010 = **2** |

Insert `0x5A` into `[15:8]` of `0xABCD1234`:

| step | value |
| --- | --- |
| m << 8 | 0x0000FF00 |
| x & ~(m << 8) | 0xABCD0034 |
| (v & m) << 8 | 0x00005A00 |
| OR | **0xABCD5A34** |

### Code
```cpp
#include <cstdint>
#include <cassert>

inline uint32_t field_mask(int hi, int lo) {
    int w = hi - lo + 1;
    return (w >= 32) ? 0xFFFFFFFFu : ((1u << w) - 1u);   // 1u << 32 is UB
}

inline uint32_t get_field(uint32_t x, int hi, int lo) {
    return (x >> lo) & field_mask(hi, lo);
}

inline uint32_t set_field(uint32_t x, int hi, int lo, uint32_t v) {
    uint32_t m = field_mask(hi, lo);
    return (x & ~(m << lo)) | ((v & m) << lo);
}

int main() {
    assert(get_field(0b11010110u, 5, 3) == 2u);
    assert(set_field(0xABCD1234u, 15, 8, 0x5A) == 0xABCD5A34u);
}
```

