**Key idea:** `static` changes **lifetime** or **sharing** depending on where it appears.

| Context | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| local variable in a function | initialized once, keeps its value between calls |
| class data member | one copy shared by all objects |
| class member function | no `this`, can only touch static members |
| namespace/file-scope variable or function | internal linkage: visible only in this translation unit |

```cpp
int next_id() {
    static int id = 0;          // initialized once (thread-safe since C++11)
    return id++;                // 0, 1, 2, ...
}

class Txn {
public:
    static int count;           // shared by all Txn objects
    Txn() { count++; }
    static int created() { return count; }
};
int Txn::count = 0;             // one definition (or 'inline static' in C++17)
```

