**Key idea:** `size_t` is **unsigned**. `i >= 0` is always true, and decrementing 0 wraps to `SIZE_MAX`, so the loop runs forever (and indexes out of bounds).

| iteration | i (64-bit size_t) | i >= 0 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ... | 1 | true |
| ... | 0 | true |
| next | 18446744073709551615 | true: out of bounds |

```cpp
vector<int> a = {1, 2, 3};

for (size_t i = a.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) { }   // BUG: infinite, UB on a[i]

// Fix 1: signed index
for (int i = (int)a.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) { }

// Fix 2: test-then-decrement idiom (handles size 0 too)
for (size_t i = a.size(); i-- > 0; ) { }

// Fix 3: reverse iterators
for (auto it = a.rbegin(); it != a.rend(); ++it) { }
```

### Follow-ups
- **Related trap:** `a.size() - 1` on an empty vector is `SIZE_MAX`, so `for (size_t i = 0; i < a.size() - 1; i++)` overflows on empty input.
- **Compiler help:** `-Wall -Wextra` warns "comparison of unsigned expression >= 0 is always true".
